ore_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.014908261819922653,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":35.1,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.08632923384766333,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":1.0982109578829669,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.012610001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":8.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"uniQure N.V. develops treatments for patients suffering from rare and other devastating diseases in the United States. The company offers HEMGENIX that allows people living with hemophilia B to produce factor IX, which can lower the risk of bleeding. Its lead product candidate is AMT-130, a gene therapy candidate, which is in Phase I/II clinical study for the treatment of Huntington's disease. The company also develops AMT-260, which is in Phase I/IIa clinical trial for the treatment of mesial temporal lobe epilepsy; AMT-162, which is in Phase I/IIa clinical trial to treat superoxide dismutase enzyme-amyotrophic lateral sclerosis; and AMT-191, an investigational gene therapy candidate which is in phase I/IIa clinical trial for the treatment of fabry disease. It has a licensing agreement with Apic Bio to develop, manufacture, and commercialize intrathecally administered investigational gene therapy for ALS caused by mutations in SOD-1; and development and commercial supply agreement with CLS Bhering. uniQure N.V. was founded in 1998 and is headquartered in Amsterdam, the Netherlands.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew Craig Kapusta CPA | CEO & Executive Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 221 people. Revenue per employee of $73K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $80K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 14\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["uniQure N.V. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.5B market cap on $16M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -47% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -110% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $178M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 110% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 1152% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"se